From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:04:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: samsung: add Google gs201 pin controller data

gs201 has nine pin controllers. FAR_ALIVE, GSACORE, GSACTRL, PERIC1 and
HSI1 share their bank layout with gs101. The others differ:

 - ALIVE: gpa2 has four pins, which shifts the filter offsets of the
   following banks;
 - PERIC0: gpp19 has five pins;
 - HSI2 has only gph2 and gph4; gph3 (the UFS pins) moved to a separate
   HSI2UFS controller.

Bank layouts are taken from Google's GPL gs201 pinctrl driver. The
wake-up interrupt numbering of ALIVE banks after gpa2 does not match the
hardware EINT numbers, which only matters for the PMU wake-up mask in
system suspend; that is left for later.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
